# Fixed 2026-11-27, defect 2876, lane runtime-names: a member's name of a
# struct the Heroes runtime's header declares, `hero_code`, bound as a
# function through `stdio.h`.
# Symptom: refused as a name `heroes_runtime.h` declares, whose functions
# free what the program holds; the header declares no `hero_code`, only a
# member of that name, which no binding can reach.
# Cause and repair: `fixedbugs-2876-the-switch-heroes-unit-h-defines-bound-through-it-is-told-as-its-macro`.
# A member's name is no name of the runtime's, so the binding is told as any
# other name `stdio.h` does not declare. Bound from a header of the
# program's own that declares it, it builds and runs:
# `tests/golden/run/fixedbugs-2876-a-members-name-of-the-runtimes-binds-a-function-of-the-programs-own`.

extern "stdio.h"
    function hero_code() -> i64  #~ ffi_unknown_name

function main()
    print(hero_code())
